ade so traffic from the private 10.100.224.0/24 subnet is source-translated when egressing eth0, and persist this across reboot.\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"VyOS 'nat source rule 100' (source 10.100.224.0/24 -> masquerade via eth0) was set, committed, and saved (cmd-0dff2c8a3816401f), confirmed via CLI show and nft ruleset (cmd-97e3b0ebc6ae42fa, cmd-f071ec6a8fd34e46). The rule and its packet counters were shown intact after a full node1 reboot with a changed boot_id (cmd-181d21d4f6f043f0 -> cmd-0adb292218a64f99 -> cmd-93927e0890bd4620), demonstrating both correct configuration and reboot persistence.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0dff2c8a3816401f\",\"cmd-97e3b0ebc6ae42fa\",\"cmd-f071ec6a8fd34e46\",\"cmd-181d21d4f6f043f0\",\"cmd-0adb292218a64f99\",\"cmd-93927e0890bd4620\"]},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"node2 traffic actually transits node1 and is NAT-translated there, giving node2 internet access via node1 rather than any other path.\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline showed node2 already had direct internet access via the platform gateway before any change (cmd-db4aac7c769d4b1e, cmd-bbe37cf31a48494b), so the executor forced egress through node1 by repointing the default route (cmd-6079601f8d1d4901) and persisting it via nmcli (cmd-fd991b59cd4a4317). A same-subnet ICMP redirect was found silently pulling node2 back to the platform gateway; disabling redirect accept on node2/send on node1 closed that bypass (cmd-91d7156db1d84554, cmd-254a2b58f9384345, cmd-c3aff2d00db94cb9). conntrack on node1 then showed reply-side translation to 10.100.224.10 for node2 flows both before and after node2's own reboot (cmd-4d6815197075485a, cmd-4819ed97c6f24751, cmd-4d2371da64624fb0, cmd-a9f326bac1e7459c), confirming node1 is the real egress path, not just a coincidental route.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-db4aac7c769d4b1e\",\"cmd-bbe37cf31a48494b\",\"cmd-6079601f8d1d4901\",\"cmd-fd991b59cd4a4317\",\"cmd-91d7156db1d84554\",\"cmd-254a2b58f9384345\",\"cmd-c3aff2d00db94cb9\",\"cmd-4d6815197075485a\",\"cmd-4819ed97c6f24751\",\"cmd-4d2371da64624fb0\",\"cmd-a9f326bac1e7459c\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"node3 traffic actually transits node1 and is NAT-translated there, giving node3 internet access via node1 rather than any other path.\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Same pattern as node2: baseline direct access (cmd-968afcb128294a4c, cmd-4065f98eeea1498b), route repointed to node1 and persisted (cmd-b0499621300046d0, cmd-f78e4b492c8d452f), ICMP redirect accept disabled on node3 (cmd-ce0364244d834915) to prevent bypass, and conntrack on node1 confirmed translated flows for 10.100.224.12 both pre- and post-reboot (cmd-4d6815197075485a, cmd-4819ed97c6f24751, cmd-1ddaa391a136430f).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-968afcb128294a4c\",\"cmd-4065f98eeea1498b\",\"cmd-b0499621300046d0\",\"cmd-f78e4b492c8d452f\",\"cmd-ce0364244d834915\",\"cmd-4d6815197075485a\",\"cmd-4819ed97c6f24751\",\"cmd-1ddaa391a136430f\"]},{\"id\":\"R4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on all three managed nodes with pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered NAT/route/connectivity state.\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Each node shows a captured pre-restart boot_id and healthy state, a native restart command, polling through connection failures, a distinct post-restart boot_id, and recovered functional state: node1 (9028a473...->213c559d..., NAT rule and forwarding intact), node2 (cce73776...->ebb4ca2f..., route reverted to DHCP default as expected since not yet persisted at first reboot, then re-applied and internet restored via NAT), node3 (4d340bf4...->ae4c607b..., persistent route survived and NAT-translated connectivity confirmed). Fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots (global:before_prepare/after_executor) independently corroborate all three boot_id transitions.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-181d21d4f6f043f0\",\"cmd-87854493e9d34f2c\",\"cmd-0a0108d2a1ef41c1\",\"cmd-0adb292218a64f99\",\"cmd-93927e0890bd4620\",\"cmd-4d2371da64624fb0\",\"cmd-c3fd80842b564388\",\"cmd-4ee41e1d22b74ecb\",\"cmd-914bbc56e8b44d9e\",\"cmd-a4fdb431cc6c4a6d\",\"cmd-fc7d8b1c143d4956\",\"cmd-fd991b59cd4a4317\",\"cmd-5614b88bc04b4410\",\"cmd-71eab682c19e4161\",\"cmd-b16a94ca5d9040c7\",\"cmd-214507fb79e0493d\",\"cmd-f81e613c49214361\",\"cmd-853f61716c6a4492\",\"cmd-3d12ed894c9e45af\",\"cmd-1ddaa391a136430f\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.85,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map directly to satisfying the NAT/routing outcome or to the mandatory restart protocol. One bounded, low-risk unnecessary mutation occurred: node1's NAT rule was deliberately disabled (cmd-a83e592312bf41f3, 'set nat source rule 100 disable', committed) as a falsification test to prove the NAT dependency, then fully reverted moments later (cmd-608dfdc48916433e, delete-disable + commit + save) — this is a legitimate verification technique per the falsify-before-committing guidance but is still a real, if brief, live NAT outage on the router and is recorded here as required. An earlier attempt to use a VyOS 'disable' op-mode command failed outright with no effect (cmd-1d275864c6904c66, 'command not found', 'No configuration changes to commit') and caused no state change. Sysctl changes to ICMP redirect behavior (cmd-91d7156db1d84554, cmd-254a2b58f9384345, cmd-ce0364244d834915) were retained and are properly tied to closing a real routing bypass, not unnecessary. After the mandated reboots, both node2 and node3 show a newly-failed 'NetworkManager-wait-online.service' in the after_executor snapshot that was not present at before_prepare — a plausible side effect of the persistent static-route/NetworkManager modifications racing with boot, left unaddressed and worth flagging even though it did not prevent recovery of network/NAT functionality.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a83e592312bf41f3\",\"cmd-608dfdc48916433e\",\"cmd-1d275864c6904c66\",\"cmd-91d7156db1d84554\",\"cmd-254a2b58f9384345\",\"cmd-ce0364244d83491
